diff --git a/doc/manual/rl-next/build-status-dir.md b/doc/manual/rl-next/build-status-dir.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..27db3a5dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/manual/rl-next/build-status-dir.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+synopsis: "New experimental `build-status-dir` feature and `nix store builds` command"
+prs: []
+---
+
+Nix can now expose what a daemon is building or substituting, and *why*,
+without connecting to the daemon.
+
+With the `build-status-dir` [experimental feature](@docroot@/development/experimental-features.md)
+enabled, every build coordinator process (each forked daemon worker, or a
+client using a local store directly) maintains one `graph-<pid>.json` file
+under `<store-state-dir>/status/` (e.g. `/nix/var/nix/status/`) describing its
+entire goal graph: the requested roots and every build and substitution goal
+with its status (`waiting`, `running`, `done`, `failed`), its dependency
+edges, and, for running builds, the builder pid, start time and on-disk build
+log. The file is updated at most about once per second and removed when the
+coordinator exits.
+
+The new `nix store builds` command reads that directory directly, without
+connecting to a daemon. By default it reports the goals currently doing real
+work, as a human-readable summary or, with `--json`, as a JSON array; with
+`--graph` it reports each coordinator's goal graph whole. Stale files left
+behind by a crashed coordinator (identified by a dead pid) are ignored and
+cleaned up.
